# Performance Rule

Read `.cursor/packs/unity-game/guides/performance.md` before writing or reviewing any per-frame code path.

Key rules (NON-NEGOTIABLE):

- Zero heap allocations in `Update`, `FixedUpdate`, and `LateUpdate`.
- Cache `GetComponent<T>()` and `Camera.main` in `Awake` — never call in `Update`.
- No LINQ on hot paths — use manual loops.
- No string concatenation on hot paths.
- Use `MaterialPropertyBlock` for per-instance color/property changes — never access `renderer.material`.
- Split UI Canvases by update frequency (HUD, Static, Popups).
- Use non-allocating physics variants: `RaycastNonAlloc`, `OverlapSphereNonAlloc`.
- Pool frequently instantiated objects — never `Instantiate`/`Destroy` in hot paths.
